  "reason": "Evidence: config_007 (avgpool + weighted fusion, pca_n2000, resnet50) achieved the best accuracy (0.639), and avgpool clearly outperforms transformer aggregation (0.639 vs 0.573 in config_008). The fusion method (weighted vs concat) is an untested design axis within the best-known architecture. This experiment tests whether concat fusion can match or exceed weighted fusion while keeping all other hyperparameters at their proven-best values (multiprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, avgpool). It is the most targeted, low-uncertainty next step: a single-variable change from the current best. If concat improves accuracy, it opens a new direction; if not, we confirm weighted fusion is optimal and can pivot to testing stronger image encoders (ViT-L) or learned RNA encoders. Expected cost: similar to config_007 (~10-11 GPU hours), since the architecture is identical except for the fusion operation (concat vs weighted average), making it a moderate-cost experiment relative to the budget."
